#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192592 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5bc2c576-4f7c-5b4a-8c78-8a41420fdcce" :knowledge-point/title "Isolating an Absolute Value Expression"}] :question/id #uuid "b3b99d07-5914-578b-9aaf-f028ada5bee0" :question/math-academy-id "e-14220" :question/problem "Consider the absolute value equation \n\n$$\n-3|1-x|-2 = -8.\n$$\n\nThis equation can be expressed in the following equivalent form:\n\n$$\n|1-x|=k\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "We can rearrange the equation to isolate the absolute value on the left-hand side:\n\nFirst, we add $2$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3|1-x|-2 & =-8 \\\\ -3|1-x|-2+2 & =-8+2 \\\\ -3|1-x| & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $-3{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3|1-x| & =-6 \\\\ \\frac{-3|1-x|}{-3} & =\\frac{-6}{-3} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-3}|1-x|}{\\cancel{-3}} & =2 \\\\ |1-x| & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192593 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192635 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "94d6a2aa-4288-51dc-8944-cf9490812ad2" :knowledge-point/title "Absolute Value Equations With No Solution"}] :question/id #uuid "89382e45-4e78-554f-88e1-2bbf281617e9" :question/math-academy-id "e-14223" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has *no* solution?\n\nI. $|1-x| = -5$\n\nII. $|1-x| + 5 = 2$\n\nIII. $|1-x| = 3$" :question/worked-solution "An absolute value equation has no solution if, when the absolute value is isolated on the left-hand side, the right-hand side is negative.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each equation in turn:\n\n- Equation I *has no solution*. The absolute value is already isolated on the left-hand side, and the right-hand side is *negative*.\n\n- Equation II *has no solution*. To see this, we first isolate the absolute value on the left-hand side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|1-x|+5 & =2 \\\\ |1-x| & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the right-hand side is *negative*, this equation has *no* solution.\n\n- Equation III has a solution. The absolute value is already isolated on the left-hand side, and the right-hand side is non-negative.\n\nTherefore, the answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192594 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192636 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "15f03573-42ee-50d4-acdf-e2ee05d3e7e4" :knowledge-point/title "Rearranging and Solving an Absolute Value Equation"}] :question/id #uuid "de2efe4f-e236-5fb2-bc46-eb037ecf26b1" :question/math-academy-id "e-14228" :question/problem "Solve the equation $2| 2a - 4 | - 7 = 13.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the absolute value on the left side of the equation:\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2|2a-4|-7 & =13 \\\\ 2|2a-4| & =20 \\\\ |2a-4| & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following two cases:\n\n- If $|2a-4| = 2a-4,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|2a-4| & =10 \\\\ 2a-4 & =10 \\\\ 2a & =14 \\\\ a & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|2a-4| = -(2a-4),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|2a-4| & =10 \\\\ -(2a-4) & =10 \\\\ -2a+4 & =10 \\\\ -2a & =6 \\\\ a & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $a=-3$ and $a=7.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487339 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5bc2c576-4f7c-5b4a-8c78-8a41420fdcce" :knowledge-point/title "Isolating an Absolute Value Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d34e6bd-f4b7-56e2-b7bb-3bf9883cc110" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486681} {:answer/id #uuid "311eb7ac-e3aa-59be-b549-8528d5bc7230" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486697} {:answer/id #uuid "7016cb28-c67c-589f-b8de-b1568482a084" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486839} {:answer/id #uuid "746316d6-9e5f-5a02-8027-eeb6602550fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486846} {:answer/id #uuid "765f2de1-fc12-5392-832e-f5d33ec11be3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486851}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d34e6bd-f4b7-56e2-b7bb-3bf9883cc110" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486681} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7933389-f875-5063-949e-56f9664cbd7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487278}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "65b91c89-ea1f-5d94-8a2d-584db112f3d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-154635" :question/problem "Consider the absolute value equation \n\n$$\n5-|x-3|=-3.\n$$\n\nThis equation can be expressed in the following equivalent form:\n\n$$\n|x-3|=k\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "We can rearrange the equation to isolate the absolute value on the left side:\n\nFirst, we subtract $5$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5-|x-3|=-3 \\\\ 5-|x-3|-5=-3-5 \\\\ -|x-3|=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we multiply both sides of the equation by $-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-|x-3| & =-8 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-|x-3|) & =(-1)\\cdot (-8) \\\\ (\\cancel{-}1)\\cdot (\\cancel{-}|x-3|) & =8 \\\\ |x-3| & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487333 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192635 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "94d6a2aa-4288-51dc-8944-cf9490812ad2" :knowledge-point/title "Absolute Value Equations With No Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15baa1d5-fba5-5eb4-ad30-a795a51c00a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486641} {:answer/id #uuid "31c4e53d-dd41-5cde-9b2d-fdf4ebcbfddc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486700} {:answer/id #uuid "6c86b89c-dead-57cf-bbd7-045b959c8168" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486831} {:answer/id #uuid "7fed39f0-5a99-5d32-aa75-49783c59e161" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486872} {:answer/id #uuid "d02b9bfd-e22f-5d02-b1ab-123317beac55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487051}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31c4e53d-dd41-5cde-9b2d-fdf4ebcbfddc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486700} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7a4bfbe-757f-5eb8-9d00-cbed8edcec34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487279}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5bd06631-7e99-59a6-a0d1-351c08d361fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-154662" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has *no* solution?\n\nI. $|2x+1|-2=3$\n\nII. $|2x+1|=1$\n\nIII. $|2x+1|=-3$" :question/worked-solution "An absolute value equation has no solution if, when the absolute value is isolated on the left side, the right-hand side is negative.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each equation in turn:\n\n- Equation I has a solution. To see this, we first isolate the absolute value on the left-hand side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|2x+1|-2 & =3 \\\\ |2x+1| & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the right-hand side is non-negative, this equation has a solution.\n\n- Equation II has a solution. The absolute value is already isolated on the left-hand side, and the right-hand side is non-negative.\n\n- Equation III *has no solution*. The absolute value is already isolated on the left-hand side, and the right-hand side is *negative*.\n\nTherefore, the answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487392 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192635 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "94d6a2aa-4288-51dc-8944-cf9490812ad2" :knowledge-point/title "Absolute Value Equations With No Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1eb2b10e-8e54-5eb1-bcba-8ce98a286647" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486652} {:answer/id #uuid "3efd5fe2-c41a-5145-b546-cd82120daef3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486731} {:answer/id #uuid "5add9119-4743-5972-a40c-1a3f0523a51c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486798} {:answer/id #uuid "7337e704-8f0e-5a54-82ec-c796a40bd0a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486844} {:answer/id #uuid "b69b8ac9-a46a-5a52-a60e-4f459186b3b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486995}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1eb2b10e-8e54-5eb1-bcba-8ce98a286647" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486652} :answer-field/id #uuid "473fd6dc-e319-5fd7-8c1c-70de7487ffef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487170}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e251dfd2-42a3-5421-a165-7d060c5b7a7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-154670" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has *no* solution?\n\nI. $|5-x|=7$\n\nII. $1-|5-x|=5$\n\nIII. $|5-x|=-1$" :question/worked-solution "An absolute value equation has no solution if, when the absolute value is isolated on the left side, the right-hand side is negative.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each equation in turn:\n\n- Equation I has a solution. The absolute value is already isolated on the left-hand side, and the right-hand side is non-negative.\n\n- Equation II *has no solution*. To see this, we first isolate the absolute value on the left-hand side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-|5-x| & =5 \\\\ -|5-x| & =4 \\\\ |5-x| & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the right-hand side is *negative*, this equation has *no* solution.\n\n- Equation III *has no solution*. The absolute value is already isolated on the left-hand side, and the right-hand side is *negative*.\n\nTherefore, the answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193245 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5bc2c576-4f7c-5b4a-8c78-8a41420fdcce" :knowledge-point/title "Isolating an Absolute Value Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "895acbd4-b75b-5e2d-8826-7504e842cc33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486893}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "895acbd4-b75b-5e2d-8826-7504e842cc33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486893} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee0c8bd5-1086-5d70-85b2-9d89fb5fe3c3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191269}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e5a53e17-d1d0-5fa9-8d04-0b459a7ec9bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-212480" :question/problem "Consider the absolute value equation \n\n$$\n2-|x+2|=-7.\n$$\n\nThis equation can be expressed in the following equivalent form:\n\n$|x+2|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We can rearrange the equation to isolate the absolute value on the left side:\n\nFirst, we subtract $2$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-|x+2|=-7 \\\\ 2-|x+2|-2=-7-2 \\\\ -|x+2|=-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we multiply both sides of the equation by $-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-|x+2| & =-9 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-|x+2|) & =(-1)\\cdot (-9) \\\\ (\\cancel{-}1)\\cdot (\\cancel{-}|x+2|) & =9 \\\\ |x+2| & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487368 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5bc2c576-4f7c-5b4a-8c78-8a41420fdcce" :knowledge-point/title "Isolating an Absolute Value Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41d3b03a-8656-5627-b2c0-840a2683ea81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486736}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41d3b03a-8656-5627-b2c0-840a2683ea81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486736} :answer-field/id #uuid "900a048e-e1a2-5ff2-a6f9-c2138bc5b41f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487217}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ad83e0ea-4391-59a0-adc0-7a2eea885dc7" :question/math-academy-id "q-215502" :question/problem "Consider the absolute value equation \n\n$$\n8-|4x+5|=1.\n$$\n\nThis equation can be expressed in the following equivalent form:\n\n$|4x+5|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We can rearrange the equation to isolate the absolute value on the left side:\n\nFirst, we subtract $8$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8-|4x+5|=1 \\\\ 8-|4x+5|-8=1-8 \\\\ -|4x+5|=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we multiply both sides of the equation by $-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-|4x+5| & =-7 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-|4x+5|) & =(-1)\\cdot (-7) \\\\ (\\cancel{-}1)\\cdot (\\cancel{-}|4x+5|) & =7 \\\\ |4x+5| & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487365 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5bc2c576-4f7c-5b4a-8c78-8a41420fdcce" :knowledge-point/title "Isolating an Absolute Value Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d36bd4c2-8bfa-5ef0-80fe-bb3a6d81eaa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487055}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d36bd4c2-8bfa-5ef0-80fe-bb3a6d81eaa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487055} :answer-field/id #uuid "bad153a8-2020-537a-b663-7fb9b6a11421" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487245}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "aacab06e-bd32-550c-b949-9f30eb343d4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-215504" :question/problem "Consider the absolute value equation \n\n$$\n-8|2x+1|+20=4.\n$$\n\nThis equation can be expressed in the following equivalent form:\n\n$|2x+1|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We can rearrange the equation to isolate the absolute value on the left side:\n\nFirst, we subtract $20$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8|2x+1|+20 & =4 \\\\ -8|2x+1|+20-20 & =4-20 \\\\ -8|2x+1| & =-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $-8:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8|2x+1| & =-16 \\\\ \\frac{-8|2x+1|}{-8} & =\\frac{-16}{-8} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-8}|2x+1|}{\\cancel{-8}} & =2 \\\\ |2x+1| & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487385 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192636 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "15f03573-42ee-50d4-acdf-e2ee05d3e7e4" :knowledge-point/title "Rearranging and Solving an Absolute Value Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e072f22c-c1b4-50bd-b169-9a43180a22c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487083}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e072f22c-c1b4-50bd-b169-9a43180a22c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487083} :answer-field/id #uuid "829441c2-76a8-59bd-9d55-9bedb13a25b2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487210} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "daacb6bf-94a8-52cd-9997-5c3176d5861d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487069}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "daacb6bf-94a8-52cd-9997-5c3176d5861d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487069} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f8cb172-8a46-5e7a-a23a-587cdf7bd723" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487228}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d1182683-804f-5b60-aecd-25a7c3c4b698" :question/math-academy-id "q-215509" :question/problem "Written in ascending order, the solutions to $|5-x|-8=7$ are $x=${{field-1}}\nand $x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the absolute value on the left side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|5-x|-8 & =7 \\\\ |5-x| & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following two cases:\n\n- If $|5-x|=5-x,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|5-x| & =15 \\\\ 5-x & =15 \\\\ -x & =10 \\\\ x & =-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|5-x|=-(5-x),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|5-x| & =15 \\\\ -(5-x) & =15 \\\\ -5+x & =15 \\\\ x & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-10$ and $x=20.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487342 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192636 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "15f03573-42ee-50d4-acdf-e2ee05d3e7e4" :knowledge-point/title "Rearranging and Solving an Absolute Value Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "134da1c6-a5fe-5aaf-877e-e7d3b0e64c90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486636}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "134da1c6-a5fe-5aaf-877e-e7d3b0e64c90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486636} :answer-field/id #uuid "4480594b-9ce7-562d-a893-9644ffee21a7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487167} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "929e62fb-c6fb-5144-932a-cfb1d9b3c7cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486915}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "929e62fb-c6fb-5144-932a-cfb1d9b3c7cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486915} :answer-field/id #uuid "70955f2b-2b9c-5dd9-b1e4-e4c8bed173b4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487201}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "75db5801-eb7a-544e-9657-7c91f7a11bf0" :question/math-academy-id "q-215513" :question/problem "Written in ascending order, the solutions to $4-|2x-5|=3$ are $x=${{field-1}} \nand $x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the absolute value on the left side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4-|2x-5| & =3 \\\\ -|2x-5| & =-1 \\\\ |2x-5| & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following two cases:\n\n- If $|2x-5|=2x-5,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|2x-5| & =1 \\\\ 2x-5 & =1 \\\\ 2x & =6 \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|2x-5|=-(2x-5),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|2x-5| & =1 \\\\ -(2x-5) & =1 \\\\ -2x+5 & =1 \\\\ -2x & =-4 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=2$ and $x=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487381 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192636 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "15f03573-42ee-50d4-acdf-e2ee05d3e7e4" :knowledge-point/title "Rearranging and Solving an Absolute Value Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "376e1aa3-5cd6-5893-b22d-6da7743dbc40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b=-11,5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486712} {:answer/id #uuid "504f560d-5e8a-51cd-8209-ee224e1274d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b=-5,12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486768} {:answer/id #uuid "51b47407-efa2-5d2a-84c4-fad6ca2e90ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b=5,11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486774} {:answer/id #uuid "a9262c0e-2abd-5bd4-8a44-567f73af36c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b=-5,11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486977} {:answer/id #uuid "f944162d-d1c0-5ad4-992f-bf106975c0b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b=-12,3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487125}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9262c0e-2abd-5bd4-8a44-567f73af36c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b=-5,11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486977} :answer-field/id #uuid "fac5256f-c4eb-5937-9a69-2c2d9a6f4b46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487281}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c8460d4b-81b8-5707-a316-5df813e7f65d" :question/math-academy-id "q-75890" :question/problem "If $|6-2b|+2=18,$ then $b=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the absolute value on the left side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|6-2b|+2 & =18 \\\\ |6-2b| & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following two cases:\n\n- If $|6-2b|=6-2b,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|6-2b| & =16 \\\\ 6-2b & =16 \\\\ -2b & =10 \\\\ b & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|6-2b|=-(6-2b),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|6-2b| & =16 \\\\ -(6-2b) & =16 \\\\ 2b-6 & =16 \\\\ 2b & =22 \\\\ b & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $b=-5$ and $b=11.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487353 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192636 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "15f03573-42ee-50d4-acdf-e2ee05d3e7e4" :knowledge-point/title "Rearranging and Solving an Absolute Value Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26888d75-42dd-5e33-82b3-e66a129d799b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2,-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486670} {:answer/id #uuid "5966e32f-f8ed-5b11-90da-c45203d5cb09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{4}{5},2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486790} {:answer/id #uuid "97368357-2d10-5f19-a263-44790d0d5834" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2,\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486933} {:answer/id #uuid "b2b44fb4-4a25-50f8-b23a-3318b59371a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{4}{5},2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486991} {:answer/id #uuid "b9b8feb3-7773-598d-b726-2945fd040832" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{2}{5},2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5966e32f-f8ed-5b11-90da-c45203d5cb09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{4}{5},2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486790} :answer-field/id #uuid "78d6d4b4-a80d-51e7-9f1e-304b3e64fdce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487205}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "99e6cc0a-d678-5e56-8a48-bdcbe16a46ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-75892" :question/problem "If $2|5x-3|+1=15,$ then $x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the absolute value on the left side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2|5x-3|+1 & =15 \\\\ 2|5x-3| & =14 \\\\ |5x-3| & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following two cases:\n\n- If $|5x-3|=5x-3,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|5x-3| & =7 \\\\ 5x-3 & =7 \\\\ 5x & =10 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|5x-3|=-(5x-3),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|5x-3| & =7 \\\\ -(5x-3) & =7 \\\\ -5x+3 & =7 \\\\ -5x & =4 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-\\frac{4}{5}$ and $x=2.$"}]}
